title: Labor Rights
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: labor_rights_timer += 10; month_actions += 1
view-if: dvp_in_government and labor_minister_party = dvp_name and labor_rights_timer <= 0
card-image: img/portraits/ThielOtto.jpg
max-visits: 6
go-to: labor_rights_menu

= Labor Rights

With control of the Labor Ministry, we can set national standards for labor. Though not our usual domain, our supporters still expect us to curtail the socialist unions and facilitate business for employers.

@labor_rights_menu

- @working_hours: Enforce the 40-hour work week.
- @safety: Reduce safety standards. 
- @target_spd_unions: Target <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span>-affiliated unions
- @unemployment_insurance: Fund the unemployment insurance program.
- @root: Do not enact any policies.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@working_hours
view-if: black_thursday_seen = 1 and return_to_normalcy = 0
on-arrival: working_hours += 1; labor_dissent -= 8; progressive_dissent -= 5; industrialist_dissent += 5; labor_strength += 5; progressive_strength += 3; workers_dvp += 5*(1-dissent); spd_relation += 4; inflation += 0.1; economic_growth -= 0.1; unemployed -= 0.2;

While a 40-hour work week was declared during the German Revolution in 1918, enforcement has become increasingly porous over the years. We have successfully added numerous exceptions and loopholes, returning to the old regime of forced overtime for workers.

Now, however, with the rising unemployement in the wake of Black Thursday, perhaps it is time to enforce these these rights in hopes of containing the crisis. This policy will be unpopular with our industrial backers and its effects are expected to be limited.


@safety
on-arrival: workers_safety -= 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government; labor_dissent += 5; progressive_dissent += 3; industrialist_dissent -= 5; industrialist_strength += 3; workers_dvp -= 3*(1-dissent)

We slowly chip away at existing safety regulations, while also turning a blind eye to violations. Employers approve of these measures, while our labor faction and our few working class supporters express their dissatisfaction.


@target_spd_unions
choose-if: spd_in_government == 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our coalition partners will not allow this.
on-arrival: labor_strength += 5; industrialist_dissent -= 5; workers_dvp += 4*(1-dissent); spd_relation -= 8; workers_spd -= 5;

We promore right-wing trade unions, mainly the [? if dfgb_formed == 0: DHV ?][? if dfgb_formed == 0: DFGB ?], as an alternative to the ADGB, successfully peeling some workers away from the <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span>. Naturally, the social democrats are displeased with us.


@unemployment_insurance
view-if: unemployed >= unemployment_insurance_threshold + 4
subtitle: With increasing unemployment, we must find new ways to fund the program.

With the onset of the Depression and its throngs of unemployed, the unemployment insurance program is under strain. It was never designed for this many claimants; something must be done to balance the budget.

- @cut_benefits: Cut benefits.
- @increase_employers: Increase employer contributions.
- @balance: Increase both employer and employee contributions.
- @labor_rights_menu: We can defer this decision for now.

@cut_benefits
subtitle: Our expected course of action.
on-arrival: coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government; workers_dvp -= 4*(1-dissent); unemployed_dvp -= 4*(1-dissent); workers_nsdap += 6; unemployed_kpd += 5; unemployed_nsdap += 5; labor_dissent += 15; progressive_dissent += 10; democratic_dissent += 5; industrialist_dissent -= 10; industrialist_strength += 10; welfare -= 2; budget += 1; unemployed += 3; pro_republic -= 4; spd_relation -= 8; inflation -= 2; unemployment_insurance_threshold = unemployed; unemployment_insurance_timer = 10; economic_growth -= 0.2;

For budgetary reasons, we have cut unemployment insurance benefits. Unfortunately, our reasons for fiscal discipline are alien to the workers. They are furious at our betrayal, as are a good portion of our membership throughout the factions. Our loss is the KPD's gain, and even the NSDAP, those lapdogs of the bourgeoisie, have joined in criticizing us for our austerity.

@increase_employers
subtitle: Employers are strongly against this.
on-arrival: capital_strike_progress += 2; welfare += 1; workers_dvp += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_dvp -= 6; new_middle_dvp -= 1; labor_dissent -= 5; labor_strength += 5; progressive_dissent -= 5; progressive_strength += 5; industrialist_dissent += 15; unemployment_insurance_threshold = unemployed; unemployment_insurance_timer = 10; economic_growth -= 0.2;

We have increased employer contributions to the unemployment insurance fund, allowing the program to continue without hurting workers and the unemployed. Predictably, our industrial backers are furious, while our small base among the workers is pleased.

@balance
subtitle: Neither workers nor employers will be entirely satisfied or dissatisfied. Our party might just weather the storm.
on-arrival: workers_dvp -= 2; workers_kpd += 4; unemployed_kpd += 3; unemployed_nsdap += 3; labor_dissent += 8; industrialist_strength += 5; welfare -= 1; budget += 1; inflation -= 1; unemployment_insurance_threshold = unemployed; unemployment_insurance_timer = 10; coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government; economic_growth -= 0.1;

Neither side is entirely satisfied by our compromise solution. Many of the industrialists see this as a betrayal, although we present it as the successful aversion of a much worse alternative.
